# DataDoctor

Read `AGENTS.md` before changing scope, UX, or code. If this rule and `AGENTS.md` disagree, `AGENTS.md` wins. Update `AGENTS.md` when a locked decision changes.

- Classification CSV tool. User picks the target, sees issues, chooses actions, downloads the working data, and trains when they want.
- Never auto-clean. Suggestions come from detector rules. Between-run text comes from saved runs plus the action log. No LLM for decisions.
- v1 model is Logistic Regression only. Baseline means the smallest trainable pipeline, not the raw dirty CSV.
- Keep original data immutable. Mutate a working copy. Row fixes apply to train only. Fit imputers and scalers on train only. Dropping a column applies to train and test.
- Leakage and bad labels are warnings. Do not silently relabel.
- The user is a beginner. Explain in plain language and do not add v1-out-of-scope features (SMOTE, extra models, AutoML, accounts, per-click undo).
- Build `notebooks/prototype.py` before Streamlit. UI code must call `data_doctor/`, not reimplement detection or training.
